From: Avery Felts <averyfelts@aol.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 08:27:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 187/188] windowscodecs: NEON premultiply, unpremultiply and
 BGR swaps.

The 32bppPBGRA and 32bppBGRA converters and reverse_bgr8, bit-exact:
- Premultiplying uses an exact division by 255; alpha 255 gives the same
  channel back, so no pixel is skipped.
- Unpremultiplying divides in float, exact for these operands, and keeps the
  low byte of results over 255 as the BYTE store does.
- reverse_bgr8 swaps 16 pixels at a time for 3 and 4 bytes per pixel.

1920x1080, ms old -> new: unpremultiply 3.06 -> 0.73, premultiply 2.17 ->
0.32, RGBA<->BGRA 0.46 -> 0.12, RGB<->BGR 0.59 -> 0.14.
